    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Lumbar plexus:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " forms within psoas major, in front of the lumbar transverse processes."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Lumbar plexus branches:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " subcostal (T12), iliohypogastric (L1), ilioinguinal (L1), genitofemoral (L1, 2), lateral femoral cutaneous (L2, 3), femoral (L2, 3, 4), obturator (L2, 3, 4), and the lumbosacral trunk (L4, 5), which joins the sacral plexus."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Lumbar plexus supply:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " motor to the lower limb and pelvic girdle; sensory to the lower anterior abdominal wall, groin, upper thigh and pudenda."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sacral plexus:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " forms on the front of piriformis where the lumbosacral trunk (L4-5) joins the ventral rami of S1 to S4."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sacral branches before the divisions:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " nerve to piriformis (S1-S2), perforating cutaneous nerve (S2-S3), posterior femoral cutaneous nerve (S1-S3), pelvic splanchnic (parasympathetic) nerves (S2-S4), pudendal nerve (S2-S4), perineal branch (S4)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sacral anterior division:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " nerve to quadratus femoris and inferior gemellus (L4-S1), nerve to obturator internus and superior gemellus (L5-S2), and the tibial part of the sciatic nerve (L4-S3)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sacral posterior division:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " superior gluteal nerve (L4-S1), inferior gluteal nerve (L5-S2), and the common peroneal part of the sciatic nerve (L4-S2)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Pudendal nerve:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " from S2-4; the nerve of the perineum and pelvic floor."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Pudendal nerve course:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " leaves the pelvis through the greater sciatic foramen below piriformis, turns around the sacrospinous ligament, passes through the lesser sciatic foramen and runs in the pudendal canal on the obturator fascia."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Pudendal nerve branches:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " inferior rectal nerve (perianal skin and external anal sphincter), dorsal nerve of the penis or clitoris, and perineal nerve (superficial and deep perineal muscles and the external urethral sphincter)."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
